    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1683">

                <pb facs="1207" n="1091" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1091"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.93/94 b.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Special Agent Carothers</hi>.<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d1683-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 27, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>At request Chinese Legation ask Villa order adequate protection extended Chinese
                    residents Guaymas, many of whose stores recently looted.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1683-f1" n="11" type="source" xml:id="d1683-f1-content">
                <p>Similar telegram to the American consul at Hermosillo.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
